<section class="reference-section" id="devi-mahishasura"><div class="reference-section-heading"><h2>Devi and Mahishasura</h2><a href="/devi-mahishasura.html">Return to story</a></div><div class="reference-content"><p><strong>Devi Mahatmya · Chapters 2–4.</strong> Original condensed prose, checked against F. E. Pargiter’s 1904 Markandeya Purana translation, transcribed at Wisdom Library, and the Sanskrit/English chapter presentation at the Devi Mahatmya Digital Temple. The corresponding Pargiter cantos are 82–84. Verse divisions can differ between presentations; chapter references are given below. Translator notes and interpretation pages are commentary, distinct from the narrative.</p><ol><li><a href="https://www.wisdomlib.org/hinduism/book/the-markandeya-purana/d/doc117157.html">Pargiter · Canto 82</a><small>Defeat of the gods, manifestation, weapons and the opening battle.</small></li><li><a href="https://devimahatmya.com/chapter-2-the-slaughter-of-mahi%E1%B9%A3asuras-armies/">Devi Mahatmya · Chapter 2</a><small>Sanskrit and English cross-check: divine radiance, gifts, lion and armies.</small></li><li><a href="https://www.wisdomlib.org/hinduism/book/the-markandeya-purana/d/doc117158.html">Pargiter · Canto 83</a><small>Commanders, buffalo form, transformations and the Goddess’s victory.</small></li><li><a href="https://devimahatmya.com/chapter-3-the-slaying-of-mahi%E1%B9%A3asura/">Devi Mahatmya · Chapter 3</a><small>Cross-check of the sequence: buffalo, lion, armed man, elephant, buffalo; spear and sword in the final encounter.</small></li><li><a href="https://www.wisdomlib.org/hinduism/book/the-markandeya-purana/d/doc117161.html">Pargiter · Canto 84</a><small>The gods’ hymn, protection, requested boon and conclusion.</small></li></ol><p>Do not import the separate Shumbha–Nishumbha or Raktabija episodes into this account. The hymn’s theology is presented as the text’s devotional praise, and the modern reflection remains editorial.</p><p>The cover is an eight-armed Durga interpretation with selected gifts. Chapter 2 also uses expansive imagery of many arms; the painting does not reproduce every textual attribute. The buffalo interior is a symbolic narrative scene, not a photograph or an exact battle tableau. Both new assets are AI-generated and each appears once.</p></div></section>
